/-- **Lemma `ext:kernel-integration`** (the measure `𝔪` on the product, for nonnegative and for
integrable complex functions).
Let $(X,\mathcal A,\lambda)$ be a sigma-finite measure space and let $z\mapsto\nu_z$ be a
measurable kernel on $\mathbb R^q$.  For every nonnegative
$\mathcal A\otimes\mathcal B(\mathbb R^q)$-measurable function $F$, the function
$z\mapsto\int F(z,\xi)\,d\nu_z(\xi)$ is measurable.  There is a sigma-finite measure
$\mathfrak m$ on the product space satisfying
